(6017908, 881615, 108580, '<td valign="top">A Rose, by any other name. Lovely soft image, a bit of grain, not serious. Decent composition. Not a lot of bokeh to be seen BEHIND the subject (i.e. Background OOF area)</td>', 'A Rose, by any other name. Lovely soft image, a bit of grain, not serious. Decent composition. Not a lot of bokeh to be seen BEHIND the subject (i.e. Background OOF area)', '2010-05-20 03:54:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6017910, 882386, 100393, '<td valign="top">A perfectly contrived cliche. I mean that in a good way; we all become aware of what we need to do to meet the demands of a challenge, and our ability (and willingness) to respond to that challenge varies. Every shot we take is contrived, in the sense that we frame it, you have gone further and constructed and controlled every element. There is an artistic honesty in that - an acknowledgement that every image is constructed, framed, chosen.<br/> <br/>Some people (including me), will see dpc cliche in this image - a water drop, super sharpness, circles of confusion; but they''ll also be aware that (like me) that they wouldn''t have the skills or patience to pull something like this off.<br/> <br/>I don''t particularly like the image - but I really admire it and the skill and commitment behind it.<br/> <br/>A 9 from me.</td>', 'A perfectly contrived cliche. I mean that in a good way; we all become aware of what we need to do to meet the demands of a challenge, and our ability (and willingness) to respond to that challenge varies. Every shot we take is contrived, in the sense that we frame it, you have gone further and constructed and controlled every element. There is an artistic honesty in that - an acknowledgement that every image is constructed, framed, chosen. Some people (including me), will see dpc cliche in this image - a water drop, super sharpness, circles of confusion; but they''ll also be aware that (like me) that they wouldn''t have the skills or patience to pull something like this off. I don''t particularly like the image - but I really admire it and the skill and commitment behind it. A 9 from me.', '2010-05-20 03:56:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6017911, 881572, 108580, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous image. Sharp (perhaps a bit too much USM), colourful, interesting. The bokeh is superb, even in all round consistency, unobtrusive and due to this makes the prime subject pop. Ladybug moved slightly and is a bit blurred thus a 9.</td>', 'Gorgeous image. Sharp (perhaps a bit too much USM), colourful, interesting. The bokeh is superb, even in all round consistency, unobtrusive and due to this makes the prime subject pop. Ladybug moved slightly and is a bit blurred thus a 9.', '2010-05-20 03:58:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6017914, 881483, 108580, '<td valign="top">Magnificent floral image, love the partial backlight seeping through and the stem in shade. Not your average flower shot. 9</td>', 'Magnificent floral image, love the partial backlight seeping through and the stem in shade. Not your average flower shot. 9', '2010-05-20 03:59:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6017916, 883454, 108580, '<td valign="top">Classic 70''s style use of a Technical Mask. Simple and appealing.</td>', 'Classic 70''s style use of a Technical Mask. Simple and appealing.', '2010-05-20 04:00:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6017917, 882659, 108580, '<td valign="top">Simple and effective. Great entry.</td>', 'Simple and effective. Great entry.', '2010-05-20 04:01:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6017924, 882076, 112828, '<td valign="top">A critique by request:<br/> <br/>I was torn on this image, between a 5 and a 6, I gave you a 5, and I''ll explain that decision, but first, let me explain why it almost got a 6..  It was fairly unique among this field of very strong entries, and it has great emotional impact.<br/> <br/>Now, why did it get the lower score?<br/> <br/>Simple, I think the B&amp;W was a questionable processing choice, and the image looks a bit too high in contrast.<br/> <br/>Your bokeh is too sharp, I much prefer a smoother softer creamy bokeh..  Still a nice image, and I was glad to see it in the challenge.</td>', 'A critique by request: I was torn on this image, between a 5 and a 6, I gave you a 5, and I''ll explain that decision, but first, let me explain why it almost got a 6..  It was fairly unique among this field of very strong entries, and it has great emotional impact. Now, why did it get the lower score? Simple, I think the B&W was a questionable processing choice, and the image looks a bit too high in contrast. Your bokeh is too sharp, I much prefer a smoother softer creamy bokeh..  Still a nice image, and I was glad to see it in the challenge.', '2010-05-20 04:13:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6017929, 881151, 108580, '<td valign="top">Great macro...perfect focus on antennae and blossoms</td>', 'Great macro...perfect focus on antennae and blossoms', '2010-05-20 04:17:07.000000', NULL, 1),
