(6018382, 883558, 92577, '<td valign="top">very nice all round, colour comp. &amp; subject</td>', 'very nice all round, colour comp. & subject', '2010-05-20 12:57:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6018387, 883372, 55956, '<td valign="top">there is a bit of sensor dust in the middle of photo</td>', 'there is a bit of sensor dust in the middle of photo', '2010-05-20 13:03:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(6018416, 881900, 17126, '<td valign="top">one of the coolest ideas here.</td>', 'one of the coolest ideas here.', '2010-05-20 13:31:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6018459, 881142, 115307, '<td valign="top">Great capture. One of the few examples I have seen where the bokeh creates drama rather than a peaceful addition of color, and does so in a way that adds to the image. I do think that the title is necessary for this one. I might find that the bokeh takes away from the image, if it wasn''t perfectly clear that the dramatic effect was intentional. Fortunately, the intention is made perfectly clear. Your squirrel is "surrounded" indeed.</td>', 'Great capture. One of the few examples I have seen where the bokeh creates drama rather than a peaceful addition of color, and does so in a way that adds to the image. I do think that the title is necessary for this one. I might find that the bokeh takes away from the image, if it wasn''t perfectly clear that the dramatic effect was intentional. Fortunately, the intention is made perfectly clear. Your squirrel is "surrounded" indeed.', '2010-05-20 14:08:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6018460, 883381, 115307, '<td valign="top">This image lacks focus for me. For bokeh to be particular effective and pleasing, there needs to be that stark contrast between completely clear and completely blurred. That contrast is missing for me here.</td>', 'This image lacks focus for me. For bokeh to be particular effective and pleasing, there needs to be that stark contrast between completely clear and completely blurred. That contrast is missing for me here.', '2010-05-20 14:10:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6018461, 882979, 115307, '<td valign="top">Beautiful image of a dandelion and an interesting take of bokeh. It seems like more of a gradient, which is interesting. The shallow DoF works wonders here</td>', 'Beautiful image of a dandelion and an interesting take of bokeh. It seems like more of a gradient, which is interesting. The shallow DoF works wonders here', '2010-05-20 14:11:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6018472, 883337, 115307, '<td valign="top">Unique Bokeh!<br/>One criticism I have here is that the person is reaching for a pawn rather than one of the back figures. THe pawn is completely hidden behind the king, so essentially it looks like the hand is grasping at nothing, which severely takes away from the effect that you were going for. I know your title tries to clarify, and my knowledge of chess clarifies as well, but the actual visual effect is not very strong. I think if the angle of the board had just been shifted slightly so that the pawn was more visibly, this would have worked better.</td>', 'Unique Bokeh!One criticism I have here is that the person is reaching for a pawn rather than one of the back figures. THe pawn is completely hidden behind the king, so essentially it looks like the hand is grasping at nothing, which severely takes away from the effect that you were going for. I know your title tries to clarify, and my knowledge of chess clarifies as well, but the actual visual effect is not very strong. I think if the angle of the board had just been shifted slightly so that the pawn was more visibly, this would have worked better.', '2010-05-20 14:15:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6018473, 881635, 115307, '<td valign="top">Very well done. This is what I love about Bokeh, you pretty much get something new every time. I am not sure I have ever admired a picture of a frog with a purple spotted background before :-)<br/>Nice clarity, composition, and use of empty space.</td>', 'Very well done. This is what I love about Bokeh, you pretty much get something new every time. I am not sure I have ever admired a picture of a frog with a purple spotted background before :-)Nice clarity, composition, and use of empty space.', '2010-05-20 14:17:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6018482, 882981, 115307, '<td valign="top">The bokeh itself is nice, but for me it doesn''t really compliment your subject very much. I can''t exactly place a finger on why, if its because the colors are too bright, or because your subject doesn''t stand out enough, or maybe something else, but it just doesn''t feel quite "right" to me. It feels like your bokeh is loud and demanding, and overwhelming your subject in this picture.<br/>Nice use of thirds rule to place your snake in this picture. 5</td>', 'The bokeh itself is nice, but for me it doesn''t really compliment your subject very much. I can''t exactly place a finger on why, if its because the colors are too bright, or because your subject doesn''t stand out enough, or maybe something else, but it just doesn''t feel quite "right" to me. It feels like your bokeh is loud and demanding, and overwhelming your subject in this picture.Nice use of thirds rule to place your snake in this picture. 5', '2010-05-20 14:21:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6018485, 883618, 115307, '<td valign="top">While your picture does have bokeh, for me it is missing a subject. In my opinion, bokeh in general (i.e. not just in your picture but in most pictures) is not strong enough to be its own subject.</td>', 'While your picture does have bokeh, for me it is missing a subject. In my opinion, bokeh in general (i.e. not just in your picture but in most pictures) is not strong enough to be its own subject.', '2010-05-20 14:23:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6018493, 882639, 115307, '<td valign="top">By far one of the better flower bokeh shots I have seen so far. Very nice colors and clarity, and the bokeh of other flowers really compliments the picture. I tried very much to accomplish the same in my image for this challenge, but did not succeed nearly as well. (I love that saying that doesn''t give anything at all away, because there are SO many flower images in this challenge :-P)</td>', 'By far one of the better flower bokeh shots I have seen so far. Very nice colors and clarity, and the bokeh of other flowers really compliments the picture. I tried very much to accomplish the same in my image for this challenge, but did not succeed nearly as well. (I love that saying that doesn''t give anything at all away, because there are SO many flower images in this challenge :-P)', '2010-05-20 14:25:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6018496, 882364, 17507, '<td valign="top">Great colors. A bit of USM would have made the foreground pop nicely.</td>', 'Great colors. A bit of USM would have made the foreground pop nicely.', '2010-05-20 14:26:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(6018507, 881338, 17507, '<td valign="top">I''m afraid this photograph gives me no particular reason to care about Joshua Brent Showalter. If there''s some logic behind your decision to focus on his grave, it doesn''t come through. As it is, it looks like a random choice of innumerable similar gravestones, with the only purpose of showing the name being an attempt to create some kind of emotional impact--which, because of its apparently arbitrary nature, does not work.</td>', 'I''m afraid this photograph gives me no particular reason to care about Joshua Brent Showalter. If there''s some logic behind your decision to focus on his grave, it doesn''t come through. As it is, it looks like a random choice of innumerable similar gravestones, with the only purpose of showing the name being an attempt to create some kind of emotional impact--which, because of its apparently arbitrary nature, does not work.', '2010-05-20 14:29:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6018508, 882989, 115307, '<td valign="top">Wow, this is truly gorgeous! The colors are gorgeous, and the "feel" is just right with a lovely mix of softness and focus. This is the kind of image that I try for, and fail at :-P. Would you mind telling me your editing steps at the end of this challenge?<br/>I do have to say that those two little petals peeking out of the left side stick out to me  like a sore thumb, but I am sure you would have fixed that if it had been advanced editing.<br/>Great job and a 9 from me :-)</td>', 'Wow, this is truly gorgeous! The colors are gorgeous, and the "feel" is just right with a lovely mix of softness and focus. This is the kind of image that I try for, and fail at :-P. Would you mind telling me your editing steps at the end of this challenge?I do have to say that those two little petals peeking out of the left side stick out to me  like a sore thumb, but I am sure you would have fixed that if it had been advanced editing.Great job and a 9 from me :-)', '2010-05-20 14:29:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6018511, 882076, 115307, '<td valign="top">This image probably would have gotten an 8 from me in a Free Study. I think it is a marvelous portrait! However, in regards to this challenge I don''t feel like the bokeh is really complimenting your subject. It certainly isn''t hurting, but it is kind of just "There". I do feel like I need to judge this photo based on the challenge at hand rather than just whether I like it or not, so I will be giving you a 6. Sorry</td>', 'This image probably would have gotten an 8 from me in a Free Study. I think it is a marvelous portrait! However, in regards to this challenge I don''t feel like the bokeh is really complimenting your subject. It certainly isn''t hurting, but it is kind of just "There". I do feel like I need to judge this photo based on the challenge at hand rather than just whether I like it or not, so I will be giving you a 6. Sorry', '2010-05-20 14:32:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6018517, 883441, 115307, '<td valign="top">Beautiful bokeh. I have always found that the most successful bokeh for flowers are more of its own in the background, and this is one such striking example. Very interesting flower, and the purple and green contrasts nicely.</td>', 'Beautiful bokeh. I have always found that the most successful bokeh for flowers are more of its own in the background, and this is one such striking example. Very interesting flower, and the purple and green contrasts nicely.', '2010-05-20 14:34:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6018604, 883610, 116105, '<td valign="top">Great picture, but I really hate that the edge of the bottle is outside of the frame.  Still 8/10 :)</td>', 'Great picture, but I really hate that the edge of the bottle is outside of the frame.  Still 8/10 :)', '2010-05-20 15:37:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6018606, 883297, 116105, '<td valign="top">Great expression!</td>', 'Great expression!', '2010-05-20 15:39:33.000000', NULL, 1);
