(6031919, 883558, 3746, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by william88:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JustCaree:</b></div><hr/><i> for educational purposes (newbie here) I am trying to figure out what you did to DQ. Im not quite understanding and dont see anything that looks off... if you are willing can you post the original or perhaps explain it to me a bit?? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>In the RAW adjustment window of Photoshop CS3, I used the "Lens Vignetting" slide bar. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I DQ`d mine for almost the same reason (I added mine in Lightroom)... pity you lost the ribbon.</td>', 'Originally posted by william88: Originally posted by JustCaree: for educational purposes (newbie here) I am trying to figure out what you did to DQ. Im not quite understanding and dont see anything that looks off... if you are willing can you post the original or perhaps explain it to me a bit??  In the RAW adjustment window of Photoshop CS3, I used the "Lens Vignetting" slide bar.   I DQ`d mine for almost the same reason (I added mine in Lightroom)... pity you lost the ribbon.', '2010-05-29 21:16:38.000000', NULL, 0),
